'''balanoid''' (bal′a̤-noid), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< Gr. βαλανοειδής, like an acorn, < βάλανος, an acorn, + εἶδος, form.] '''I.''' ''a.'' Resembling an acorn: specifically applied to the acorn-shells of the family ''Balanidæ.'' See cut under ''Balanus.''

'''II.''' ''n.'' An acorn-shell; a cirriped of the family ''Balanidæ.''

'''Balanoidea''' (bal-a̤-noi′dē-ä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Balanus'' + ''-oidea.'' Cf. ''balanoid.''] Same as ''Balanidæ.''

